# ✅ **Subordinating Conjunctions – Detailed Guide**

---

## 🔹 **What is a Subordinating Conjunction?**

A **Subordinating Conjunction** is a word or group of words that joins a **dependent clause (subordinate clause)** to an **independent clause (main clause)**.

📌 It shows a **relationship** such as:

* Time (समय)
* Cause (कारण)
* Condition (शर्त)
* Purpose (उद्देश्य)
* Contrast (विरोध)
* Place (स्थान)
* Comparison (तुलना)

---

## 🧾 **Main Subordinating Conjunctions by Category**

| 🔸 **Category**         | 🔸 **Conjunctions**                                            | 🔸 **Hindi Meaning** | 🔸 **Example Sentence**                               |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| **Time**                | after, before, when, while, as, until, since, once, as soon as | जब, पहले, बाद, तक    | I went out **after** I finished my work.              |
| **Cause/Reason**        | because, since, as, now that                                   | क्योंकि, चूंकि       | I stayed home **because** it was raining.             |
| **Purpose**             | so that, in order that                                         | ताकि                 | She works hard **so that** she can pass.              |
| **Condition**           | if, unless, provided that, in case                             | अगर, जब तक नहीं      | You can't go out **unless** you finish your homework. |
| **Contrast/Concession** | although, though, even though, whereas, while                  | हालांकि, जबकि        | **Although** it was raining, they played outside.     |
| **Comparison**          | than, as...as, as if, as though                                | से, जैसे कि          | He is taller **than** his brother.                    |
| **Place**               | where, wherever                                                | जहाँ, जहाँ भी        | Go **wherever** you want.                             |
| **Result**              | so that, such...that                                           | इतना कि              | He ran **so fast that** no one could catch him.       |

---

## 🧱 **Sentence Structure**

There are two main ways to use subordinating conjunctions:

### 🔸 1. Main Clause + Subordinating Conjunction + Subordinate Clause

* I will call you **when I reach home**.
* She left the party **because she was tired**.

### 🔸 2. Subordinate Clause + , + Main Clause

* **Because she was tired**, she left the party.
* **Although it was raining**, we went outside.

