## 🧠 **Explanation of Some Important Subordinating Conjunctions**

### 🔸 **Because** – shows reason

📌 I was late **because** I missed the bus.
👉 क्यों? – क्योंकि मैंने बस मिस कर दी

---

### 🔸 **Although / Though / Even though** – shows contrast

📌 **Although** he is rich, he is not happy.
👉 वह अमीर है, फिर भी खुश नहीं है

---

### 🔸 **If / Unless** – shows condition

📌 **If** you study hard, you will pass.
📌 You won’t pass **unless** you study hard.
👉 अगर नहीं पढ़ोगे तो पास नहीं होगे

---

### 🔸 **Until / Till** – up to a point in time

📌 Wait **until** I come back.
👉 जब तक मैं वापस न आ जाऊँ, तब तक रुको

---

### 🔸 **Since** – from a point in time

📌 I have been working **since** morning.
👉 सुबह से काम कर रहा हूँ

---

### 🔸 **While** – during the same time or contrast

📌 She was singing **while** he was playing the guitar.
📌 He is very active, **while** his brother is lazy.

---

## ❌ **Common Errors**

| ❌ Wrong Sentence                       | ✅ Correct Sentence                     |
| -------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| I will go because you will come.       | I will go **if** you come. (condition) |
| He is poor although he is honest.      | He is **honest although** he is poor.  |
| Unless you don’t work, you won’t pass. | **Unless** you work, you won’t pass.   |

